New features introduced in this update include 13 additional JavaScript modules and a new CSS file. Each script initializes a new module, logs its loading status, and appends a message to a content area in the HTML. Developers can test these changes by including the scripts in their HTML file and checking for console logs and DOM updates in the specified content area. To utilize the new styles, link the styles.css file in the head section of your HTML. No additional configuration is required apart from ensuring that the content area with the ID 'content' exists in your HTML document.